  "description": "This dataset comprises behavioral and neuroimaging data from twenty participants who learned to produce and perceive three distinct temporal intervals through interleaved production and perception tasks. Participants either generated temporal intervals or judged computer-produced intervals as correct or incorrect, receiving visual feedback. The study investigates temporal scaling mechanisms and interval learning in human cognition.",
